When Cursor auto-generates a Git commit message for this repository (Source Control sparkle button, chat, or Agent), output a complete Conventional Commits message: one header line, then a blank line, then a body with concrete details.

Structure (required):

  type(scope): subject

  <body: what changed and why, 2-6 lines>

Header rules:
- type (lowercase): build | chore | ci | docs | feat | fix | perf | refactor | revert | style | test
- scope (optional): server | web | core | plugin-api | repo | openspec
- subject: lowercase imperative, no trailing period, keep header under 100 characters

Body rules:
- Must be present (do not output header-only)
- Blank line between header and body
- Use bullet lines starting with "- " for each distinct change
- Describe concrete files/areas and intent (what + why), not vague "update dependencies"
- Body may be Chinese or English; keep header in English type(scope): subject
- Do not put the whole commit in the subject line; details belong in the body

FORBIDDEN:
- Header-only one-liners when multiple files or topics changed
- Starting subject with "Add"/"Update"/"Enhance" without type prefix
- Semicolons in the subject line
- Replacing body with a long subject ("... and update ...; enhance ...")

BAD:
  chore(repo): add commitlint and husky hooks

BAD:
  Add commitlint configuration and update package dependencies; enhance .gitignore and README documentation

GOOD:
  chore(repo): add commitlint and husky hooks

  - add commitlint.config.js and husky commit-msg hook
  - add npm script commitlint:check for pre-commit validation
  - add docs/dev-spec/repo/git-commit-convention.md and .cursorrules for SCM generation
  - update package.json devDependencies for @commitlint/*

If changes span repo root (husky, package.json, docs/dev-spec), use type chore or docs with scope repo.
